# Where the in-game AddOn List files this addon. Without a Category it lands
# under the catch-all at the bottom, which is where every addon that never set
# one ends up. The per-locale lines are the client's own category names, so a
# French or German client files it under its own word rather than the English
# one -- the addon's own translations are a separate thing and cover fewer
# languages than this does.
## Category: Chat
## Category-enUS: Chat
## Category-deDE: Chat
## Category-esES: Chat
## Category-esMX: Chat
## Category-frFR: Discussion
## Category-itIT: Chat
## Category-koKR: 대화
## Category-ptBR: Bate-papo
## Category-ruRU: Чат
## Category-zhCN: 聊天
## Category-zhTW: 對話

# Libraries
Libs\LibStub\LibStub.lua
Libs\CallbackHandler-1.0\CallbackHandler-1.0.lua
Libs\LibUIDropDownMenu\LibUIDropDownMenu.lua

# Core Lua
Locales.lua
SocialPlus.lua

# Modules split out of SocialPlus.lua, loaded after it.
#
# After it, not before: they call into functions the main file defines, and a
# Lua file runs top to bottom as it loads. Anything moved here has to be
# self-contained at load time -- registering handlers and defining functions,
# never reaching for state the main file has not built yet.
SocialPlus_Favorites.lua
SocialPlus_Who.lua
SocialPlus_Version.lua
SocialPlus_Settings.lua
SocialPlus_FriendMenu.lua
SocialPlus_Init.lua

# The /spsim friend-list simulator is not loaded at the moment.
#
# SocialPlusSim.lua is still in the repository and still in .pkgmeta's ignore
# list; only the line that loaded it is gone. To bring it back, restore:
#
#     #@do-not-package@
#     SocialPlusSim.lua
#     #@end-do-not-package@
#
# Both halves matter -- the packager strips that block, so the shipped .toc never
# points at a file the release does not contain.
#
# Why it went: a CurseForge install into the Mists client deleted the file (the
# release does not carry it) and a later mirror of this .toc put the line back,
# so the client had a .toc naming a file that was not there and reported
# "Error loading SocialPlus/SocialPlusSim.lua" at every login.
